From ab6ed945ea7af07fabdc2b72d674bc148962bde1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harrison Bowden <hbow1001@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 09:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Wire CustomizationContext.setModifier into Squoosh
 renderer

The setModifier(nodeName, ...) API was a no-op: getModifier was never
read by the squoosh renderer, and ComponentReplacementContext.layoutModifier
was hardcoded to an empty Modifier. Modifiers (theme, animation, etc.)
couldn't propagate to nested components, forcing teams to write full
component replacements instead of using the generated Kotlin code.

SquooshChildComposable now carries an optional customModifier, populated
from customizations.getModifier(view.name) at every construction site
(component replacement, scroll view, content replacement, list widget,
interactive node). SquooshRoot appends it to the per-child wrapper
modifier and exposes it as ComponentReplacementContext.layoutModifier.

Also adds FetchFigmaDocTask: a Gradle task that wraps the fetch CLI and
auto-extracts node queries from @DesignComponent / @DesignVariant
annotations in Kotlin source.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
