From 632aee095ac0bc01ba1b56012d0b6c18fde9a83a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harrison Bowden <hbow1001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 10:47:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Render modifier-wrapped subtrees via sub-SquooshRoot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1 wired customizations.getModifier into the renderer, but
modifier-only nested nodes (no replacement, scroll, list, or
interaction) aren't their own composables in Squoosh — visuals are
drawn by the parent's draw block. Putting a Modifier on the wrapping
Layout had nothing to apply against, so alpha/graphicsLayer/animations
on @Design(node="X") modifier params still didn't take effect (issue
google/automotive-design-compose#2456).

When a node has a registered modifier and isn't already handled by a
more specific case, add it to composableList with renderSubtree=true
and skipComposableList=true. The parent draw block defers rendering
via needsChildRender, and the child composable is a sub-SquooshRoot
rooted at that node. The user's Modifier on the wrapping Layout now
wraps actual rendered pixels.

To prevent infinite recursion, RootRecurseParams gains
isModifierWrapComponent (set by withModifierWrapping()) and
resolveVariantsRecursively skips the wrap branch when this is true at
the entry of a wrap-spawned subtree. Children of that root re-enable
the wrap branch normally.
