From 6eb40531372f825f431b4c16963e38888c2272dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harrison Bowden <hbow1001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 11:52:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Drop duplicate getModifier wiring from Phase 1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream Fix #2292 (#2426) landed a getModifier let-block that does
the same job as our Phase 1 .then(child.customModifier ?: Modifier).
After the merge, both fired, double-applying the user's Modifier on
each composable child wrapper (e.g., Modifier.alpha(0.5f) became
0.25 alpha).

Remove our line. The customModifier field stays — it is still used
to expose the modifier as ComponentReplacementContext.layoutModifier
and to discriminate the renderSubtree branch added in Phase 2.
